  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (image_only, resnet50) is only 20.8%, confirming RNA is the dominant modality. The only RNA encoder tested so far is PCA (a linear method), so we have no evidence about whether a learned nonlinear representation (e.g., scVI) could improve RNA-based classification. Question: config_004 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) isolates exactly one variable—the RNA encoder—against config_001, cleanly testing whether a learned latent representation outperforms PCA in the same single-profile, RNA-only setting. Why this is best: With a limited budget, the highest-leverage question is whether we can improve the dominant modality's representation before investing in multiprofile aggregation, alternative image encoders, or multimodal fusion. A clean encoder comparison (scvi_n200 vs. pca_n2000, all else held constant) reduces the most important uncertainty with a single experiment, and the result will directly inform whether to pursue learned encoders in subsequent multiprofile or multimodal configurations."
}

